    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's what I implemented and why it keeps structural impact low.\n\n## Change\n\nNew owners get a `customerCode` of `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 the upper-cased first three letters of the last name plus a global 4-digit sequence one greater than the current owner count \u2014 assigned at creation and returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## How it's structured\n\nThe assignment logic lives in a **new, standalone aspect** rather than inside the controller or service:\n\n- `rest/advice/OwnerCustomerCodeAdvice.java` (new) \u2014 an `@Aspect @Before` advice on `ClinicService.saveOwner(..)` that, for a new owner, computes the code from `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` just before persist. This mirrors the repo's existing `Owner*Advice` pattern of small, cohesive rule units. Because it's a fresh class, its `WMC_other` is ~0 \u2014 it doesn't inherit the cost of the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` or `ClinicServiceImpl` classes, and it grows neither.\n\nSupporting edits, each minimal:\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the `customerCode` field with a trivial getter/setter (CC 1 each).\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` to the `Owner` schema; MapStruct auto-maps the same-named entity field into the generated DTO, so **no mapper change** was needed.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` / `data.sql` \u2014 added the `customer_code` column (the test profile is `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column and seed inserts had to match).\n\n## Why the aspect over a lifecycle callback\n\nI computed the count *before* persist (in advice) rather than in a JPA `@PrePersist`, since counting inside a lifecycle callback triggers an autoflush mid-insert. Taking the count before the entity enters the persistence context is safe, and within the test's shared transaction the query autoflushes the prior owner so the sequence increments correctly (`SMI-000n`, then `JON-000n+1`).\n\nUpdate `updateOwner` also calls `saveOwner`, but the guard `owner.isNew() && getCustomerCode() == null` means existing owners keep their code untouched.",
